Package: genfw
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${perl:Depends}, iptables, iproute2
Description: generate an iptables firewall from a simple rules file
 genfw builds a complete iptables ruleset from a short configuration file
 describing each network interface as internal, dmz, or outside, plus a
 few flags such as nat, trusted, or allow=ssh/tcp. It derives per-interface
 chains, every interface-to-interface path, NAT, anti-spoofing drops, and
 rate-limited logging, with a default-deny policy.
 .
 The output is in iptables-restore format and is loaded atomically. Two
 systemd units run it before the network comes up and again after, and
 dispatcher hooks rerun it when an interface appears later.
